00:00:00.530 --> 00:00:02.740
- [Instructor] So we have
four different compounds here,

00:00:02.740 --> 00:00:05.030
and we also have their molar masses

00:00:05.030 --> 00:00:06.770
and what I would like you to do

00:00:06.770 --> 00:00:10.860
is think about which of these
compounds has the highest,

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:15.720
highest percentage of sulfur by mass.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.910
So pause this video and see
if you can figure that out.

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:25.060
All right, now one way to approach this

00:00:25.060 --> 00:00:29.030
is to say for each of these compounds,

00:00:29.030 --> 00:00:31.640
so if we say per mole

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:35.610
of each compound,

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:37.213
of each compound,

00:00:38.150 --> 00:00:41.850
we could figure out how
many grams, I would say

00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:43.520
what is the mass,

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:46.870
what is the mass of sulfur

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:50.210
divided by the total mass of the compound?

00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:54.080
Total, total mass of the compound.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:55.840
Now the mass of sulfur,

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:59.780
we can see that for a mole
of each of these compounds,

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:02.750
you have exactly one mole of sulfur.

00:01:02.750 --> 00:01:03.990
In all of these formulas,

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:06.180
you see exactly one sulfur.

00:01:06.180 --> 00:01:07.870
So in all of these situations,

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:11.560
the mass of sulfur is
going to be the same.

00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:13.700
This is going to be the same,

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:17.430
same for all compounds.

00:01:17.430 --> 00:01:19.790
It wouldn't be the same for all compounds

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:21.400
if some of them had two sulfurs

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.410
or some of them had three

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:23.690
or maybe some of them had none,

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:25.350
but all of them have one sulfur,

00:01:25.350 --> 00:01:27.840
so for a mole of each of these compounds,

00:01:27.840 --> 00:01:29.950
you're going to have a mole of sulfur,

00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:33.200
and so they're going to have
the same mass of sulfur.

00:01:33.200 --> 00:01:35.310
We could take out a periodic table

00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:37.100
and we could look it up
and we could say, oh, look.

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:40.130
The average atomic mass of sulfur is 32.06

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:41.970
and so if I had a mole of it,

00:01:41.970 --> 00:01:44.150
it would be 32.06 grams,

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:47.730
so we could put the 32.06
grams up here, if we like.

00:01:47.730 --> 00:01:52.360
This would be 32.06 grams

00:01:52.360 --> 00:01:54.300
in all of these cases 'cause once again,

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:55.830
if you have a mole of
each of these compounds,

00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:56.980
you're going to have a mole of sulfur

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:59.540
because you only see one sulfur in these,

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:01.500
in each of these formulas,

00:02:01.500 --> 00:02:04.040
but the big picture is
in all of the cases,

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:05.940
I'm gonna have the same
value in the numerator,

00:02:05.940 --> 00:02:08.830
so I want to have the highest percentage,

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:12.810
I would want to minimize the
value in the denominator.

00:02:12.810 --> 00:02:14.410
So I would really want to see which one

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:16.270
would have the lowest denominator,

00:02:16.270 --> 00:02:18.340
or which one would have the lowest mass

00:02:18.340 --> 00:02:19.580
for a mole of the molecules

00:02:19.580 --> 00:02:20.800
or another way of thinking about it,

00:02:20.800 --> 00:02:23.680
which of them will have
the lowest molar mass?

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:25.720
And you could see very clearly

00:02:25.720 --> 00:02:27.730
that this compound right over here

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:30.750
has the lower, lowest molar mass.

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:32.060
So we're done.

00:02:32.060 --> 00:02:35.600
This has the highest
percentage of sulfur by mass

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:38.170
because per mole, it has
the same mass of sulfur

00:02:38.170 --> 00:02:39.310
as everything else,

00:02:39.310 --> 00:02:41.776
but it has the lowest total mass,

00:02:41.776 --> 00:02:43.840
so it's gonna have the
highest percentage of sulfur.

00:02:43.840 --> 00:02:44.980
So a quick way to do it,

00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:47.200
we just looked at the lowest molar mass.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.760
You could have gone and taken 32.06

00:02:49.760 --> 00:02:51.220
and divided by each of these values

00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:52.070
and figured out a percentage.

00:02:52.070 --> 00:02:53.890
Well, they're not asking us
to figure out the percentage.

00:02:53.890 --> 00:02:56.180
They're saying which one
has the highest percentage?

00:02:56.180 --> 00:02:59.253
And that would be this second
compound right over there.

